      "content": "That shift from AI routing to fixed-timer smart lights is a step back in efficiency. AI routing is dynamic and adapts to real-time traffic data, optimizing flow. Fixed-timer lights don't adjust to traffic conditions and could lead to increased congestion, longer travel times, and possibly higher emissions due to idling. Given the complexity of today's traffic patterns and the need for responsive systems, reverting to fixed-timer lights could degrade the efficiency of our current infrastructure. It's an unfortunate decision that may need a thorough reconsideration.",
